  "narrative": {
    "intro": "Detyens Shipyards has $261M in federal contract obligations year to date for FY2026. Detyens Shipyards has 22 awards this year, with an average award size of $11.9M, and obligations are up 9.4% year over year. Fiscal-year obligations show variability across the last six years: FY21 $96.5M, FY22 $143M, FY23 $91.7M, FY24 $121M, FY25 $239M, and FY26 $261M. The Department of Defense is the largest buyer of Detyens Shipyards, obligating $204M so far this fiscal year. The Department of Homeland Security follows with $42.1M, and the Department of Commerce follows with $14.9M. Current-year totals are partial and represent fiscal year to date obligations rather than full-year totals. The company’s FY2026 to date activity reflects larger award sizes on average, given the reported $11.9M average award and the concentration of obligations with a few top buyers. Contractors and partners evaluating opportunities with Detyens Shipyards should note the concentration in defense and homeland security agencies and the recent year-over-year increase in obligations.",
